"text": "All gates run on the Windows host through the harness. The mutation entries are host-scoped `--file` runs over files that carry no `#[cfg]` body outside tests by construction (steps 1-6). Under folded CARRY 5 (E1) each can therefore expect 0 missed on the host; the leg verdict of record stays the pre-push/CI union. The boot smoke is unchanged in shape: `boot` still passes `--cli-version 2.1.0`, so its instance runs with `cli_verified:false`, and it proves the gate step leaves start-up whole. Boot step 4 is the tail's. The live recording is an OPERATOR entry. It spends tokens and rewrites committed fixtures, so the reader never re-runs it. It needs the installed `claude` on PATH, whose non-priming liveness probe (`claude --version`) precedes it."
}
